# 2. Back-End Classes

## User Class

The `User` class represents a registered user of the application.

### Attributes

| Attribute | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| id | UUID | Unique user identifier |
| firebaseUid | String | ID provided by Firebase Authentication |
| username | String | Public username |
| email | String | User email address |
| city | String | User city or community |
| bio | String | Optional profile description |
| avatarUrl | String | Optional profile image URL |
| createdAt | Date | Date when the user was created |
| updatedAt | Date | Date when the user was last updated |

### Methods

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| updateProfile(data) | Updates the user profile information |
| getPublicProfile() | Returns public user information only |

### Example

```javascript
class User {
  constructor(id, firebaseUid, username, email, city, bio, avatarUrl) {
    this.id = id;
    this.firebaseUid = firebaseUid;
    this.username = username;
    this.email = email;
    this.city = city;
    this.bio = bio;
    this.avatarUrl = avatarUrl;
    this.createdAt = new Date();
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  updateProfile(data) {
    this.username = data.username || this.username;
    this.city = data.city || this.city;
    this.bio = data.bio || this.bio;
    this.avatarUrl = data.avatarUrl || this.avatarUrl;
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  getPublicProfile() {
    return {
      id: this.id,
      username: this.username,
      city: this.city,
      bio: this.bio,
      avatarUrl: this.avatarUrl
    };
  }
}
```

