## Book Class

The `Book` class represents a book listing created by a user.

### Attributes

| Attribute | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| id | UUID | Unique book identifier |
| ownerId | UUID | ID of the user who owns the book |
| title | String | Book title |
| author | String | Book author |
| description | String | Optional book description |
| condition | String | Book condition: new, good, used, damaged |
| exchangeType | String | Type: lend, give, exchange |
| status | String | Availability: available, reserved, unavailable |
| imageUrl | String | Book image URL |
| createdAt | Date | Date when the listing was created |
| updatedAt | Date | Date when the listing was last updated |

### Methods

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| createListing(data) | Creates a new book listing |
| updateListing(data) | Updates book information |
| markReserved() | Changes book status to reserved |
| markAvailable() | Changes book status to available |
| markUnavailable() | Changes book status to unavailable |

### Example

```javascript
class Book {
  constructor(id, ownerId, title, author, description, condition, exchangeType, imageUrl) {
    this.id = id;
    this.ownerId = ownerId;
    this.title = title;
    this.author = author;
    this.description = description;
    this.condition = condition;
    this.exchangeType = exchangeType;
    this.status = "available";
    this.imageUrl = imageUrl;
    this.createdAt = new Date();
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  updateListing(data) {
    this.title = data.title || this.title;
    this.author = data.author || this.author;
    this.description = data.description || this.description;
    this.condition = data.condition || this.condition;
    this.exchangeType = data.exchangeType || this.exchangeType;
    this.imageUrl = data.imageUrl || this.imageUrl;
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  markReserved() {
    this.status = "reserved";
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  markAvailable() {
    this.status = "available";
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  markUnavailable() {
    this.status = "unavailable";
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }
}
```

