## ExchangeRequest Class

The `ExchangeRequest` class represents a request sent by one user for a book.

A request can be for borrowing, receiving, or exchanging a book.

### Attributes

| Attribute | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| id | UUID | Unique request identifier |
| bookId | UUID | ID of the requested book |
| requesterId | UUID | ID of the user sending the request |
| ownerId | UUID | ID of the book owner |
| requestType | String | Type: borrow, give, exchange |
| status | String | pending, accepted, rejected, cancelled, completed |
| message | String | Optional first message |
| createdAt | Date | Date when the request was created |
| updatedAt | Date | Date when the request was last updated |

### Methods

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| accept() | Accepts the request |
| reject() | Rejects the request |
| cancel() | Cancels the request |
| complete() | Marks the request as completed |

### Example

```javascript
class ExchangeRequest {
  constructor(id, bookId, requesterId, ownerId, requestType, message) {
    this.id = id;
    this.bookId = bookId;
    this.requesterId = requesterId;
    this.ownerId = ownerId;
    this.requestType = requestType;
    this.status = "pending";
    this.message = message;
    this.createdAt = new Date();
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  accept() {
    this.status = "accepted";
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  reject() {
    this.status = "rejected";
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  cancel() {
    this.status = "cancelled";
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }

  complete() {
    this.status = "completed";
    this.updatedAt = new Date();
  }
}
```

