# 3. Service Components

Services contain the main business logic of the application.

| Service | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| AuthService | Verifies Firebase tokens and connects Firebase users to Livract users |
| UserService | Creates, retrieves, and updates user profiles |
| BookService | Manages book creation, update, deletion, and search |
| RequestService | Handles book requests and request status changes |
| MessageService | Handles messages inside request conversations |
| UploadService | Handles image URL validation or image storage logic |

---

## AuthService

### Responsibilities

- Verify Firebase authentication tokens.
- Check if a Firebase user already exists in the database.
- Create a Livract profile for new users.
- Protect private API routes.

---

## UserService

### Responsibilities

- Get the current user profile.
- Update user profile information.
- Return public user profiles.
- Prevent duplicate emails or usernames if required.

---

## BookService

### Responsibilities

- Create a book listing.
- Get all available books.
- Search books by title or author.
- Filter books by condition, exchange type, or status.
- Update a book listing.
- Delete a book listing.
- Check if the current user owns a book before editing or deleting it.

---

## RequestService

### Responsibilities

- Create a request for a book.
- Prevent users from requesting their own books.
- Prevent requests for unavailable books.
- Accept or reject requests.
- Update book status when a request is accepted.
- Retrieve sent and received requests.

---

## MessageService

### Responsibilities

- Send a message inside a request.
- Retrieve messages for a request.
- Check that the user is part of the request before allowing access to messages.

