# 9. Data Validation Rules

## User Validation

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| firebase_uid | Required and unique |
| username | Required |
| email | Required and unique |
| city | Required |
| bio | Optional |
| avatar_url | Optional |

---

## Book Validation

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| owner_id | Required and must reference an existing user |
| title | Required |
| author | Required |
| condition | Must be `new`, `good`, `used`, or `damaged` |
| exchange_type | Must be `lend`, `give`, or `exchange` |
| status | Must be `available`, `reserved`, or `unavailable` |
| image_url | Optional |

---

## Request Validation

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| book_id | Required and must reference an existing book |
| requester_id | Required and must reference an existing user |
| owner_id | Required and must reference an existing user |
| requester_id | Cannot be the same as owner_id |
| request_type | Must be `borrow`, `give`, or `exchange` |
| status | Must be `pending`, `accepted`, `rejected`, `cancelled`, or `completed` |

---

## Message Validation

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| request_id | Required and must reference an existing request |
| sender_id | Required and must reference an existing user |
| content | Required and cannot be empty |

---

# 10. Summary

The Livract MVP is structured around four main entities:

| Entity | Purpose |
|---|---|
| User | Represents a registered member of the community |
| Book | Represents a book shared by a user |
| ExchangeRequest | Represents a request to borrow, receive, or exchange a book |
| Message | Represents communication between users about a request |

The system uses:

- **React Native** for the mobile front-end;
- **Node.js and Express.js** for the back-end API;
- **PostgreSQL** for relational data storage;
- **Firebase Authentication** for user authentication;
- **Firebase Storage or Cloudinary** for book images.

This design is simple, scalable, and appropriate for the first MVP version of Livract.
